WEBVTT

00:09:29.273 --> 00:09:31.942
And this story, Mylo's story,

00:09:31.984 --> 00:09:35.529
is just one small example
in a much broader movement.

00:09:35.571 --> 00:09:36.864
It's the one I know.

00:09:36.905 --> 00:09:38.198
But in the last few years,

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.576
countless scientists have joined us

00:09:40.576 --> 00:09:43.203
in this journey of a sustainable
materials revolution.

00:09:43.704 --> 00:09:44.955
And in the coming years,

00:09:44.997 --> 00:09:47.082
I think we're going to see
amazing advances

00:09:47.082 --> 00:09:50.628
that replace all the harmful
materials in your closet,

00:09:50.669 --> 00:09:52.504
in your home and your car.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.967
And my hope is that,
by sharing this journey with Mylo,

00:09:57.009 --> 00:09:59.553
it can act as a blueprint
that these others can follow

00:09:59.595 --> 00:10:02.890
to more quickly improve
this world for all of us.